tant;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: Process, Redemption and Selling First</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in New Mexico</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales sale</li><li>Turn the New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a New Mexico House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>When property tax goes unpaid in New Mexico, the statutes allow the taxing authority to sell a lien or the property itself, and they give the owner a set time to redeem.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>New Mexico&#x27;s Taxation and Revenue Department Property Tax Division sells delinquent real property at public auction (NMSA 7-38-65), usually at the county courthouse. (NM TRD, Delinquent Property Tax Auctions; <a href='https://www.tax.newmexico.gov/businesses/property-tax-overview/delinquent-property-tax-auctions/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A sale properly made under 7-38-67 constitutes full payment of delinquent taxes, penalties and interest; the sale extinguishes only the tax lien, not other liens. (NM TRD, Delinquent Property Tax Auctions; <a href='https://www.tax.newmexico.gov/businesses/property-tax-overview/delinquent-property-tax-auctions/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The former owner has a two-year period to challenge the sale in court under 7-38-70; the only redemption period is the 120-day federal IRS redemption period. (NM TRD, Delinquent Property Tax Auctions; <a href='https://www.tax.newmexico.gov/businesses/property-tax-overview/delinquent-property-tax-auctions/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in New Mexico?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy New Mexico houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-mexico-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>New Mexico Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-mexico-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>New Mexico Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-mexico-guides-by-city-and-county/'>New Mexico guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-new-mexico/'>We buy houses in New Mexico</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.tax.newmexico.gov/businesses/property-tax-overview/delinquent-property-tax-auctions/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>NM TRD, Delinquent Property Tax Auctions</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"New Mexico\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-new-mexico/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-mexico-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "New Mexico Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales", "rank_math_description": "New Mexico tax deed and tax lien sales: who runs the sale, interest, redemption periods and selling before the sale. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "new mexico tax deed sales"}]